cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jam-actions-acoustic-v0 — grounded LLM tool use over audio analysis"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "mcp-tool-shop-org"
  - family-names: "Krueger"
    given-names: "Bernd"
    affiliation: "piano-midi.de (upstream MIDI arrangements; CC-BY-SA-3.0-DE)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: "CC-BY-SA-3.0-DE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mcp-tool-shop-org/ai-jam-sessions"
abstract: >-
  108 multi-turn tool-use records over ACOUSTIC music analysis, the counterpart to
  jam-actions-v0's symbolic-music traces. Each record pairs a deliberately
  perturbed synthetic rendering of a public-domain phrase with the verdict the
  analysis tools actually return, so every label is checked against the
  instrument rather than only against itself. Nine perturbation kinds per phrase
  per target note, including the two cases a naive model answers confidently and
  wrongly: a vibrato note whose correct verdict is in tune, and silence whose
  correct verdict is nothing to grade. Held out by phrase, not by record.
keywords:
  - music-information-retrieval
  - tool-use
  - audio-analysis
  - pitch-detection
  - onset-detection
  - model-context-protocol
